Claw agent
==========
A terminal-based agent(Development phase)

Currently implemented features
------------------------------
* chat <config> <promtp>  -- Interact with a large language model once
* hello <name> <age>  -- Stdout your name and age
* sum Vec<number> -- Calculate the sum of multiple numbers
* repeat <content> -- Repeat your content
* version -- Stdout the Claw version
* wait <number> -- Wait a few seconds
* read-config <config.toml> -- Read the current configuration and output it
* divide <number> <number*> -- Divide the two numbers
* fetch <website> -- fetch the head of the website
* journal -- In the journal folder, there are explanations about the other files.

Additional information
----------------------
* openai.rs -- This file extends the functionality of the chat.rs to support API processing
* test ------ chat_cli.rs -- Integration testing of the chat function
          |
          |
          --- fetch_cli.rs -- Integration testing of the fetch function
* mod.rs -- Exporting all commands is outdated; for simplicity, we'll continue using mod. In fact, the lib is the better choice
* config.rs -- Enter the LLM configuration here
* cli.rs -- Handle the execution of all commands
* main.rs -- Main entry point also handles errors

How to use it currently
-----------------------
You need to have the Rust compiler and the Cargo package manager
Clone this repository to your local machine
Use "cargo run command <parameter>" to debug this program; dependencies will be downloaded upon the first run, so there is no need to worry
You can use "cargo test" to run tests; these include both unit tests and integration tests

How to get involved in development
-----------------------------------
Feel free to submit Issues if you encounter any bugs or have any questions
You can contribute to this project by forking the repository and submitting a branch; however, please contact me before making any contributions.
My email address is listed on the homepage

Future expectations for this repository
---------------------------------------
I will continue to maintain this repository; my goal is to build a product with capabilities comparable to Codex or Grokbuild.
